From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Mitchell <me@gmitch215.xyz>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:24:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: read the siginfo pointer from the signal frame

__libc_handle_signal pushed one constant too many before the load of
info_param, so on wasm32 it loaded from address 8 instead of the frame
and left the stack pointer on the operand stack (valid only because the
function ends in unreachable). info_param was whatever sat at address 8,
zero in practice, so every SA_SIGINFO handler, thread cancellation's
among them, was called as handler(sig) and trapped on its signature.
---
48:	iLONG.const 4
diff --git a/src/signal/wasm/restore.S b/src/signal/wasm/restore.S
index a3b2abf..a15a8a5 100644
--- a/src/signal/wasm/restore.S
+++ b/src/signal/wasm/restore.S
@@ -45,7 +45,6 @@ __libc_handle_signal:
 
 	/* info_param */
 	global.get __stack_pointer
-	iLONG.const 4
 	INSN_32_64(i32.const 4, i64.const 8)
 	iLONG.add
 	iLONG.load 0
